class ConceptSystem {
  definition {
    A structured set of concepts established according to the relations
    between them, each concept being determined by its position in
    the set (ISO 12620 A.7.1).

    Promoting concept systems from implicit (the relation graph) to
    explicit first-class entities enables:
      - Concept-system-level navigation in concept-browser (the
        entire measurement-standard system as one navigable unit)
      - ISO 12620 A.7.2 concept position queries (broader /
        superordinate / subordinate / coordinate / related) as
        first-class operations
      - ISO 10241-1 §5.1 systematic-order rendering of terminological
        entries (preferred over alphabetical)
      - Aligns Glossarist with the standard's explicit modeling

    Storage: per-file at `concept-systems/<id>.yaml`, mirroring the
    relations/ pattern.

    Multidimensionality: a concept can appear in multiple concept
    systems; the same concept occupies different positions in each.
  }
  +id: String [1] {
    definition {
      Stable identifier, dataset-unique. Kebab-case recommended.
    }
  }
  +name: <<BasicDocument>> LocalizedString [1] {
    definition {
      Human-readable name, localized per ISO 639.
    }
  }
  +type: ConceptSystemType [1] {
    definition {
      The type of concept system. Per ISO 12620 A.7.1, the dominant
      relation type determines the system type. Mixed systems are
      common in real datasets.
    }
  }
  +domain: <<StandardDocument>> ReferenceToTermbase [0..1] {
    definition {
      Optional subject-area classification.
    }
  }
  +purpose: <<BasicDocument>> LocalizedString [0..1] {
    definition {
      What this concept system is for (e.g., "to define the
      components of measurement standards").
    }
  }
  +members: <<StandardDocument>> ReferenceToTermbase [1..*] {
    definition {
      All concepts in the system. Concepts may appear in multiple
      systems; the same concept occupies different positions in each.
    }
  }
  +hyperedges: <<StandardDocument>> ReferenceToTermbase [0..*] {
    definition {
      References to n-ary hyperedges (PartitiveHyperedge,
      GenericHyperedge, SequentialHyperedge) that belong to this
      system. References point to the per-file hyperedge $id.
    }
  }
  +root_concepts: <<StandardDocument>> ReferenceToTermbase [0..*] {
    definition {
      Top-level concepts in the system — those with no superordinate
      or comprehensive in this system. A system may have multiple
      roots if it spans multiple independent hierarchies.
    }
  }
  +sources: ConceptSource [0..*] {
    definition {
      Bibliographic provenance for the system itself.
    }
  }
  +status: ConceptStatus [0..1] {
    definition {
      Lifecycle status of the concept system.
    }
  }
}
